<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Oil prices are rising again. Brent crude, =
the international benchmark for oil, is up 1% this morning to $114 a barrel=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Richard Hunter of the broker Interactive I=
nvestor said that oil is now up by about 60% since the start of the Iran wa=
r, and up about 90% in the year so far.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">He said: =E2=80=9CWidespread reports that =
the US is considering renewed military strikes on Iran after the midterm el=
ections rather than pursuing a diplomatic route was enough for the price to=
 pop, after what many had considered would be a brief conflict is now in it=
s eighth month.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A fresh wave of selling hit AI stocks arou=
nd the world overnight, as investors grow increasingly anxious around the s=
ustainability of AI-fuelled returns.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Japanese and South Korean stock market=
s, which have been buoyed up by their exposure to the AI investment boom, f=
ell before recovering some ground to trade broadly flat on the day.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In the US the blue chip S&amp;P 500 fell b=
y 1.2%, its worst performance since July, and the tech-heavy Nasdaq dropped=
 by 2.6%, its biggest drop since June. The Philadelphia semiconductor index=
 fell by a painful 6.7%, also its worst day since June.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Retail sales in Great Britain fell by =E2=
=81=A00.4% in September, compared with expectations of a drop of 0.1%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">An unseasonably warm start to the autumn w=
eighed on =E2=81=A0online clothing vendors, =E2=81=A0and =E2=80=8Bsupermark=
ets also reported a drop in volumes, official figures showed.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Economists are warning there could be more=
 gloom ahead for retailers as they enter into the crucial final quarter of =
the year =E2=80=93 which includes Christmas.</p>
